/*  Unions — `(number or text)`, `is a`, narrowing, and judging by type.

    ★ A closed union is a tagged struct, a member for each case. Its cases are kept SORTED, so
      `(cat or dog)` and `(dog or cat)` are one C type, and a case's tag is its place in that order.

    ★ NARROWING IS THE CHECKER'S. It writes the type a narrowing gives a read onto the read
      (`:NarrowedType`), a judgement's `it` included, and the compiler only reaches that type from
      the kind the name is stored as: a voidable's value, a union's case member, or the smaller
      union a group of tests leaves, converted to. It used to work every narrowing out again from
      the same syntax, as C#'s compiler did — a second copy of every rule (ROADMAP, rules-twice).

    ★ The emitter's `kinds` map carries two more things per name, so every block that puts kinds
      back as they were puts these back too: `@<name>` — the C a name is read as, where that is not
      its own (a captured one, through its environment) — and `%<name>` — the kind it is stored as.
      `%return` is the kind a function gives back.

    ★ A value is WRAPPED wherever it flows into a union-typed place — a `Define` declared so,
      `becomes`, an argument, `Return`, a field, a series' items.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind fact to is-union, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "union of ".
    Done.

    /// A union's cases, in their sorted order.
    Bind series of text to kind-cases, given (the text kind):
        Define cases as a series of text.
        For each written in (the characters from 10 to the end of kind) split by "|", repeat:
            Insert written into cases.
        Done.
        Return cases.
    Done.

    /// A union kind for some cases: flattened, without repeats, sorted.
    Bind text to union-kind-of, given (the series of text cases):
        Define seen as a map from text to fact.
        Define kept as a series of text.
        For each written in cases, repeat:
            If cast is-union on (written):
                For each inner in cast kind-cases on (written), repeat:
                    If (the entry for inner in seen) is void:
                        In seen, the entry for inner becomes true.
                        Insert inner into kept.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise if (the entry for written in seen) is void:
                In seen, the entry for written becomes true.
                Insert written into kept.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define ordered as kept sorted.
        If the number of ordered is 1, return item 1 of ordered.
        Define joined-cases as "".
        For each written in ordered, repeat:
            If joined-cases is "", the joined-cases becomes written.
            Otherwise, the joined-cases becomes "{joined-cases}|{written}".
        Done.
        Return "union of {joined-cases}".
    Done.

    /// A case's tag: its place in the union's sorted cases, from 0, or -1 when it is none of them.
    Bind number to case-tag, given (the text union, the text written):
        Define place as 0.
        For each inner in cast kind-cases on (union), repeat:
            If inner is written, return place.
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        Return -1.
    Done.

    Bind text to union-c-name, given (the text kind):
        Define named as "cun".
        For each inner in cast kind-cases on (kind), repeat:
            Define part as inner.
            If cast object-of on (inner) is not "", the part becomes "obj_{cast c-ident on (cast object-of on (inner))}".
            The named becomes "{named}_{part}".
        Done.
        Return named.
    Done.

    /// A union's struct, how a case is wrapped into it, and how it is written and compared.
    Bind text to c-union-helpers, given (the text kind):
        Define type-c as cast union-c-name on (kind).
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert "typedef struct \{ int tag;" into out.
        Define place as 0.
        For each inner in cast kind-cases on (kind), repeat:
            Insert " {cast c-type on (inner)} case_{place};" into out.
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        Insert " \} {type-c};\n" into out.
        The place becomes 0.
        Define writes as a chase.
        Define tests as a chase.
        For each inner in cast kind-cases on (kind), repeat:
            Insert "static {type-c} {type-c}_from_{place}({cast c-type on (inner)} v) \{ {type-c} u; memset(&u, 0, sizeof u); u.tag = {place}; u.case_{place} = v; return u; \}\n" into out.
            Insert " case {place}: {cast write-call on (inner, "u.case_{place}")}; break;" into writes.
            Insert " case {place}: return {cast c-equal on (inner, "a.case_{place}", "b.case_{place}")};" into tests.
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        Insert "static void {type-c}_write({type-c} u) \{ switch (u.tag) \{{writes converted to text} \} \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static int {type-c}_eq({type-c} a, {type-c} b) \{ if (a.tag != b.tag) return 0; switch (a.tag) \{{tests converted to text} \} return 0; \}\n\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// Notes a union type the program uses, so its struct is written.
    Bind void to register-union unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        // A voidable of a number, a text, a fact or bits is in every program already.
        If cast is-voidable on (kind) and (cast is-scalar on (cast voidable-inner on (kind)) or cast voidable-inner on (kind) is "bits"), return.
        If cast is-union on (kind) is false and cast is-voidable on (kind) is false, return.
        If (the entry for kind in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for kind becomes true.
            Insert kind into one's union-order.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A value of kind `from` as one of kind `wanted`: wrapped into a union, converted from a
    /// smaller union, or as it is.
    Bind text to c-coerce unto emitter, given (the text value, the text source-kind, the text wanted):
        If source-kind is wanted, return value.
        If cast is-voidable on (wanted), return cast one's c-into-voidable on (value, source-kind, wanted).
        If cast is-failable on (wanted), return cast one's c-into-failable on (value, source-kind, wanted).
        If cast is-union on (wanted) is false, return value.
        Cast one's register-union on (wanted).
        Define wanted-c as cast union-c-name on (wanted).
        If cast is-union on (source-kind) is false:
            Define tag as cast case-tag on (wanted, source-kind).
            If tag < 0, return value.
            Return "{wanted-c}_from_{tag}({value})".
        Done.
        // One union into a wider one: each of its cases to the same case there.
        Define from-c as cast union-c-name on (source-kind).
        Define converting as "(\{ {from-c} cf_u = {value}; {wanted-c} cf_w; memset(&cf_w, 0, sizeof cf_w); switch (cf_u.tag) \{".
        Define place as 0.
        For each inner in cast kind-cases on (source-kind), repeat:
            Define tag as cast case-tag on (wanted, inner).
            If tag is not less than 0, the converting becomes "{converting} case {place}: cf_w = {wanted-c}_from_{tag}(cf_u.case_{place}); break;".
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        Return "{converting} \} cf_w; \})".
    Done.

    /// An expression as C, as a value of the kind a place wants.
    Bind text or failure to c-of-as unto emitter, given (the node expression, the text wanted):
        Define value as cast one's c-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define source-kind as cast one's kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Return cast one's c-coerce on (value, source-kind, wanted).
    Done.

    // ── Narrowing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The kind a name is stored as, however it is narrowed now.
    Bind text to stored-kind unto emitter, given (the text name):
        Define stored as the entry for "%{name}" in one's kinds.
        If stored is not void, return stored.
        Return the entry for name in one's kinds but void is "".
    Done.

    /// A name read as the type the checker narrowed it to: its kind, then its C — or nothing, where no
    /// narrowing reached the read.
    Bind series of text or failure to narrowed-read unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define marked as cast keyed-field on (expression, ":NarrowedType").
        If marked is void, return a series of text.
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)).
        Define to-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (marked) or pass the failure off.
        Define stored as cast one's stored-kind on (name).
        Define held as the entry for "@{name}" in one's kinds but void is "".
        If held is "", the held becomes cast c-name on (name).
        // A judgement's `void` arm has nothing to reach: it reads as it is held.
        If to-kind is stored or to-kind is "void", return a series of text with (stored, held).
        // A voidable narrowed past void reads as its value — and then, if it holds a union, within it.
        Define base as stored.
        If cast is-voidable on (stored):
            The held becomes "({held}).value".
            The base becomes cast voidable-inner on (stored).
            If to-kind is base, return a series of text with (to-kind, held).
        Done.
        If cast is-union on (base) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {stored} narrowed to a {to-kind}")).
        If cast is-union on (to-kind) is false:
            Return a series of text with (to-kind, "({held}).case_{cast case-tag on (base, to-kind)}").
        Done.
        If to-kind is base, return a series of text with (to-kind, held).
        Return a series of text with (to-kind, cast one's c-coerce on (held, base, to-kind)).
    Done.

    /// A copy of the kinds, to put back when an arm ends.
    Bind map from text to text to kinds-kept unto emitter:
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Return kept.
    Done.

    /// `If`, each arm a block of its own. What a test narrows, the checker wrote onto the reads.
    Bind void or failure to emit-if unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define first-arm as true.
        For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define condition as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (arm, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            If first-arm, cast one's line on ("if ({condition}) \{").
            Otherwise, cast one's line on ("\} else if ({condition}) \{").
            The first-arm becomes false.
            Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body) is false:
            Cast one's line on ("\} else \{").
            Cast one's emit-block on (otherwise-body) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.

    /// `Judge <a union>, where it is:` by type — a tag test for each arm. What `it` reads as in an arm,
    /// the checker wrote onto each read of it.
    Bind void or failure to emit-judge-union unto emitter, given (the node statement, the text subject-kind):
        Define subject as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define value as cast one's c-of on (subject) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        Define kept-outer as cast one's kinds-kept.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Cast one's line on ("{cast union-c-name on (subject-kind)} cv_it = {value};").
        In one's kinds, the entry for "it" becomes subject-kind.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%it" becomes subject-kind.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "@it" becomes "".
        Define first-arm as true.
        For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Define named as (cast field-of on (arm, 1))'s children.
            If the number of named is 0, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a judgement arm of values on a union")).
            Define arm-cases as a series of text.
            For each written in named, repeat:
                Insert cast one's kind-of-type on (written) or pass the failure off into arm-cases.
            Done.
            Define arm-kind as cast union-kind-of on (arm-cases).
            Define tests as "".
            Define tested as a series of text.
            If cast is-union on (arm-kind), the tested becomes cast kind-cases on (arm-kind).
            Otherwise, insert arm-kind into tested.
            For each inner in tested, repeat:
                Define test as "cv_it.tag == {cast case-tag on (subject-kind, inner)}".
                If tests is "", the tests becomes test.
                Otherwise, the tests becomes "{tests} || {test}".
            Done.
            If first-arm, cast one's line on ("if ({tests}) \{").
            Otherwise, cast one's line on ("\} else if ({tests}) \{").
            The first-arm becomes false.
            Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
        If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body) is false:
            If first-arm, cast one's line on ("\{").
            Otherwise, cast one's line on ("\} else \{").
            The first-arm becomes false.
            Cast one's emit-block on (otherwise-body) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If first-arm is false, cast one's line on ("\}").
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept-outer.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `<value> is a <type>` — a test of a union's tag; on anything else, known as it is written.
    Bind text or failure to c-type-check unto emitter, given (the node condition):
        Define target as cast field-of on (condition, 1).
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define tested as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (condition, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define negated as (cast field-of on (condition, 3))'s word is "true".
        If cast is-union on (held) is false:
            Define same as held is tested.
            If same is not negated, return "1".
            Return "0".
        Done.
        Define target-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define tests as "".
        Define tested-cases as a series of text.
        If cast is-union on (tested), the tested-cases becomes cast kind-cases on (tested).
        Otherwise, insert tested into tested-cases.
        For each inner in tested-cases, repeat:
            Define test as "cf_t.tag == {cast case-tag on (held, inner)}".
            If tests is "", the tests becomes test.
            Otherwise, the tests becomes "{tests} || {test}".
        Done.
        Define checked as "(\{ {cast union-c-name on (held)} cf_t = {target-c}; ({tests}); \})".
        If negated, return "(!{checked})".
        Return checked.
    Done.

    /// `is` / `is not` with a union on either side: the same case, holding equal values.
    Bind text or failure to c-union-equal unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define left-side as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define right-side as cast field-of on (expression, 3).
        Define left-kind as cast one's kind-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-kind as cast one's kind-of on (right-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define left as cast one's c-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define right as cast one's c-of on (right-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define equal as "".
        If left-kind is right-kind:
            The equal becomes cast c-equal on (left-kind, left, right).
        Done.
        Otherwise if cast is-union on (left-kind) and cast case-tag on (left-kind, right-kind) is not less than 0:
            Define tag as cast case-tag on (left-kind, right-kind).
            The equal becomes "(\{ {cast union-c-name on (left-kind)} cf_e = {left}; cf_e.tag == {tag} && {cast c-equal on (right-kind, "cf_e.case_{tag}", right)}; \})".
        Done.
        Otherwise if cast is-union on (right-kind) and cast case-tag on (right-kind, left-kind) is not less than 0:
            Define tag as cast case-tag on (right-kind, left-kind).
            The equal becomes "(\{ {cast union-c-name on (right-kind)} cf_e = {right}; cf_e.tag == {tag} && {cast c-equal on (left-kind, "cf_e.case_{tag}", left)}; \})".
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("comparing a {left-kind} with a {right-kind}")).
        Done.
        If (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word is "NotEqual", return "(!{equal})".
        Return equal.
    Done.
Done.
